// Max's Rage - granted fresh by BerserkSkillData.Begin every Overdrive activation and removed at
// End. Stacks builds from landed weapon hits (DamageUtility.ApplyDamage ->
// RageOverdriveUtility.TryAdvanceStack) up to MaxStacks - a pure counter/condition with NO baked-in
// stat effect of its own (see docs/max-ascensions.md's own note on why the old "single correction
// multiply at max stacks" mechanic was removed as part of the Ascension refactor). Whether Max is
// "at max Rage" is purely a live boolean condition (RageOverdriveUtility.IsAtMaxRage) that Ascensions
// (Full Throttle, Ignition) read and react to on their own - reaching max Rage does not create a
// third major stat state by itself. Taking damage resets Stacks back to 0 (MaxOverdriveReactionSystem's
// OnHealthDamageApplied/OnShieldDamageApplied reaction -> RageOverdriveUtility.ResetStacks) unless the
// entity carries RageRetentionUpgrade below (Last Stand rank 1).
component RageOverdrive
{
    Byte Stacks;
    Byte MaxStacks;
}

// Marker tag for Last Stand rank 1 ("Unshaken") - checked via f.Has<T>, same idiom as
// Invulnerable/Burrowed/Decoy. Renamed from RageOverdriveImmunity/the old standalone "Rage Overdrive"
// Hero Ascension it used to belong to - that pick no longer exists on its own, folded into Last Stand.
component RageRetentionUpgrade
{
}
